# Generated data files: never let Git attempt a textual merge on these.
#
# Everything under data/*.json is produced by a script (publish_cpurnsa.py,
# run_all_logs_refresh.py, publish_softs_diagnostics.py, etc.) from source
# CSVs/Parquet, not written by hand. A line-based git merge/rebase on two
# divergent versions of one of these files can leave content that is
# individually well-formed but structurally wrong - e.g. duplicated fields
# inside one JSON object, which happened on 2026-09-22 and broke
# cpurnsa.html in production.
#
# The "merge" driver below always reports a conflict instead of attempting
# a line-based merge, the same way Git treats binary files. This forces a
# stop instead of a silent or partial merge. To resolve a conflict on one
# of these paths: do NOT hand-edit the conflict markers. Re-run the file's
# generator against the current inputs and `git add` the fresh output.
#
# This intentionally does not use `merge=ours`: that driver resolves
# conflicts silently by keeping the local side and discarding the incoming
# side, which for files updated by automated cron/CI jobs could silently
# drop real pipeline data. `merge=binary` always stops and asks instead.
data/cpurnsa_curve_history.json merge=binary
data/cpurnsa_daily_commentary.json merge=binary
data/cpurnsa_pca_diagnostics.json merge=binary
data/health.json merge=binary
data/uscpi_release_manifest.json merge=binary
data/softs_diagnostics.json merge=binary
